# Root build-context ALLOWLIST. Two images build with the repo ROOT as their context:
#   - ops-controller (services/ops-controller/Dockerfile: COPYs ordo/ catalog/ services/)
#   - worker         (services/worker/Dockerfile: COPYs services/worker/ +
#                     services/v1-parity/dashboard/ modules it imports)
# Everything else is excluded so the context stays tiny and no operator material
# (out/secrets.env, auth/caddy/certs/, data/, models/) can ever reach the daemon.
# (Subdirectory build contexts that set their own context dir are NOT affected:
# a .dockerignore only applies to the context directory it sits in.)
*
!ordo/
!catalog/
!services/
# Re-exclude heavy gitignored/build artifacts the !services/ allowlist would otherwise pull into
# the root context (worker + ops-controller builds) — chiefly the dashboard's ~54M frontend
# node_modules and any built dist/. Keeps the context tiny and the images reproducible.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
